WEBVTT

00:05.410 --> 00:07.980
Someone let that Void into the town.

00:08.860 --> 00:10.340
What are you talking about?

00:10.340 --> 00:12.460
The one during the harvest festival.

00:12.820 --> 00:16.450
Someone cast transformation magic on it
 to make it look like the priest.

00:16.450 --> 00:20.820
Meaning that someone 
who can use magic led that Void in.

00:21.170 --> 00:24.830
You mean there's a traitor in the town?

00:25.100 --> 00:26.300
Who knows?

00:26.720 --> 00:27.450
Hey, Natsuko.

00:27.450 --> 00:28.510
Huh? Uh, yes?

00:28.510 --> 00:31.970
Did you see anything in that 
prophetic dream you call a "moo-vee"?

00:33.040 --> 00:34.470
Memmeln!

00:34.470 --> 00:36.130
Are you headed out?

00:36.130 --> 00:39.340
Yes. I have choir practice today.

00:39.340 --> 00:41.590
Wanna ride on my back?

00:41.590 --> 00:42.850
No, thank you.

00:44.260 --> 00:46.600
Wow, what a nice day.

00:46.600 --> 00:48.350
Maybe I'll go for a walk.

02:23.990 --> 02:28.500
Episode 4: ETERNITY

02:30.670 --> 02:33.170
<i>In the movie, </i>A Tale of Perishing<i>,</i>

02:33.950 --> 02:38.550
<i>mages used a transformation spell 
on a Void to make it look like the priest,</i>

02:38.930 --> 02:41.300
<i>then led it to the Soul Future tower.</i>

02:43.690 --> 02:45.810
<i>Luke managed to see through the spell.</i>

02:46.470 --> 02:49.230
<i>But then, the Ultimate Void appeared...</i>

02:51.630 --> 02:53.470
<i>and Luke defeated it.</i>

02:53.830 --> 02:54.990
<i>But it turned out to be...</i>

02:56.860 --> 02:59.530
<i>Memmeln transformed by a magic spell.</i>

03:00.210 --> 03:04.230
<i>We never get to see what 
she was trying to do in the movie,</i>

03:05.740 --> 03:07.440
<i>so it's a huge mystery.</i>

03:07.440 --> 03:12.970
<i>Her being in a choir wasn't mentioned in the 
reference sheets, either. Maybe it's connected.</i>

03:12.970 --> 03:15.020
<i>If that part that makes 
no sense comes up—</i>

03:15.020 --> 03:16.660
Why are you following Memmeln?

03:17.870 --> 03:19.540
I-I'm not following her.

03:19.540 --> 03:20.660
Memmel—

03:20.890 --> 03:22.440
Okay, okay!

03:22.440 --> 03:24.250
I saw it in the movie.

03:24.250 --> 03:27.430
They're the ones who let 
that thing into the Last Town.

03:27.430 --> 03:29.300
Memmeln did? But why?

03:29.300 --> 03:31.690
Well, no one has any idea why.

03:32.010 --> 03:34.430
That's what I'm going to find out.

03:40.690 --> 03:45.210
Memmeln has been fighting 
alongside us to protect the Last Town.

03:45.480 --> 03:49.080
I know. There must be 
some reason behind this.

03:51.840 --> 03:53.340
Huh? They're gone.

03:54.010 --> 03:55.680
Did we lose them?

03:55.680 --> 03:59.900
I'd heard the choir practiced
 in a cemetery, but...

04:00.680 --> 04:03.770
The statue of the hero 
that protects the Last Town.

04:04.160 --> 04:07.160
Dang, it's huge.

04:07.160 --> 04:10.770
Man, if I only had my smartphone, 
I'd take a photo to commemorate this.

04:13.870 --> 04:15.180
Ooh.

04:17.240 --> 04:20.000
See? It's just the choir practicing.

04:39.530 --> 04:43.220
I hate tomorrow.

04:43.220 --> 04:48.560
How long is this hell going to continue?

04:48.560 --> 04:54.490
Please just end it already.

04:54.490 --> 05:03.250
Nothingness! Nothing... ness, ness, ness...

05:05.280 --> 05:07.300
<i>Wh-What the hell?</i>

05:07.300 --> 05:09.280
<i>This scene wasn't in the movie.</i>

05:13.460 --> 05:16.540
Apparently, this summoning
ritual is also incorrect.

05:17.160 --> 05:18.290
<i>Memmeln!</i>

05:18.290 --> 05:24.910
Perhaps we really do need the Voids to eat 
the Soul Future for the Ultimate Void to appear?

05:24.910 --> 05:28.050
We were so close at the harvest festival.

05:29.810 --> 05:34.590
Lady Memmeln's idea to transform the Void
with magic to resemble the priest was brilliant.

05:34.590 --> 05:37.960
Maybe we should do that <i>one</i> ritual?

05:39.510 --> 05:41.310
Perhaps.

05:41.310 --> 05:44.310
We need Memmeln to decide on that.

05:46.920 --> 05:49.230
That ritual is the final resort.

05:49.770 --> 05:52.500
Now is not yet the time for that.

05:52.500 --> 05:55.200
Let us come up with another plan.

05:55.400 --> 05:57.220
<i>Last resort?</i>

05:57.220 --> 05:59.330
O Ultimate Void,

05:59.330 --> 06:05.080
please guide us so that we may 
one day bask in your glory.

06:05.530 --> 06:06.580
Ultimate Void!

06:06.920 --> 06:08.300
Ultimate Void!

06:09.600 --> 06:10.590
Memmel—

06:11.110 --> 06:12.590
What do you think you're doing?!

06:13.760 --> 06:15.820
Were you planning to go berserk in there?

06:15.820 --> 06:20.070
Memmeln's trying to awaken 
the Ultimate Void. We must stop her.

06:20.070 --> 06:21.350
How?

06:22.270 --> 06:23.630
How?

06:23.630 --> 06:24.790
Luke?

06:25.240 --> 06:26.360
Unio?

06:26.360 --> 06:29.270
Natsuko! What the heck are you doing here?

06:29.270 --> 06:30.180
Memmeln is—

06:30.180 --> 06:32.420
A walk! We're taking a stroll!

06:32.420 --> 06:35.120
And what are you doing up there, Unio?

06:35.120 --> 06:40.160
You know damn well if you tell Unio something,
 the whole town will know before the day is out.

06:40.160 --> 06:42.910
There'll be mass panic 
if folks find out about this.

06:42.910 --> 06:47.180
I'm here 'cause I heard the choir 
practices somewhere around here.

06:48.130 --> 06:49.800
Uh, what is it?

06:49.800 --> 06:53.270
I know! Why don't we go 
have some milk beers?

06:53.270 --> 06:54.980
Why right now?

06:54.980 --> 06:57.300
Hey! That's a great idea! Let's do that!

06:57.300 --> 07:01.300
Hey, wait! Wait, wait, wait, wait!

07:05.670 --> 07:08.220
I couldn't possibly drink any more.

07:10.780 --> 07:13.600
So what are we gonna do about Memmeln?

07:13.600 --> 07:15.550
I'll do something about it.

07:16.030 --> 07:17.940
"Something"?

07:22.450 --> 07:24.630
Absolutely not!

07:26.270 --> 07:30.640
Y-You really shouldn't go 
near Memmeln, Luke...

07:31.720 --> 07:32.640
Why not?

07:33.020 --> 07:36.960
Well, <i>you</i> know. 
You're sorta unpredictable at times.

07:36.960 --> 07:40.440
And if you go near Memmeln, 
um, uh... M-Memmeln... um...

07:38.900 --> 07:40.070
What?

07:41.290 --> 07:43.520
You might kill her.

07:43.520 --> 07:46.000
What?! Are you stupid?

07:46.000 --> 07:48.040
There's no <i>way</i> I'd kill Memmeln!

07:48.040 --> 07:51.580
<i>I</i> will do something about this, 
so you don't need to do anything.

07:51.580 --> 07:53.350
We're supposed to be comrades.

07:53.350 --> 07:57.470
Well, I've seen the movie and 
memorized all the character profile stuff.

07:57.470 --> 08:00.210
I know way more about this
 than you do, Luke.

08:00.210 --> 08:02.090
I need to stop this before it happens—

08:02.790 --> 08:07.320
Listen here. I've been with Memmeln 
way longer than you have.

08:07.320 --> 08:10.780
I know plenty of things about her
 you don't know, either.

08:10.780 --> 08:13.540
Okay, quiz time. What's Memmeln's real name?

08:13.540 --> 08:16.210
Huh? Her real name?

08:16.210 --> 08:19.580
What's this? Do you seriously not know?

08:19.580 --> 08:22.340
Three. Two. One.

08:22.340 --> 08:23.670
Memmeln the Third!

08:23.670 --> 08:27.600
Bzzt! The correct answer is Mem Meln.

08:26.020 --> 08:29.530
<b>Mem Meln</b>

08:26.020 --> 08:29.530
<b>Mem Meln</b>

08:27.600 --> 08:29.520
You just added a pause!

08:30.890 --> 08:34.960
I know a lot of things you don't, Mr. Hero.

08:35.360 --> 08:38.630
Leave this to me, and stay put.

08:39.280 --> 08:41.110
Sh-Shut up!

08:41.110 --> 08:42.360
I'm the hero here!

08:42.360 --> 08:43.910
<i>I'll</i> do something about it!

08:43.910 --> 08:47.250
You can just shut up and draw 
or whatever, you dumb anneemator!

08:47.250 --> 08:51.500
Oh? All righty then. Let's see what you've got.

08:52.020 --> 08:54.390
Stare.

08:59.280 --> 09:00.520
What's this?

09:00.520 --> 09:03.110
I thought you might like something sweet.

09:03.310 --> 09:06.350
<i>He really thinks he can solve this with food?</i>

09:08.690 --> 09:09.890
<i>It </i>is<i> good, though.</i>

09:16.470 --> 09:19.270
The weather's been nice lately.

09:29.360 --> 09:32.210
How are things going with the choir?

09:33.640 --> 09:35.080
What do you mean?

09:35.080 --> 09:38.910
Oh, uh, I just mean you seem 
to be practicing a lot lately.

09:38.910 --> 09:40.680
What kind of songs do you sing?

09:42.720 --> 09:44.480
Just normal songs.

09:46.970 --> 09:49.000
Well, you know...

09:49.630 --> 09:52.900
If you have any problems 
with the Nine Soldiers,

09:52.900 --> 09:56.480
or if anything's troubling you,
 please tell me.

09:56.880 --> 09:58.450
Nothing comes to mind.

10:03.000 --> 10:05.000
Gah! I can't take it anymore!

10:05.000 --> 10:08.120
Memmeln, when did you 
become an Ultimate Void stan?

10:08.120 --> 10:09.060
"Stan"?

10:09.060 --> 10:09.880
"Stan"?

10:09.880 --> 10:11.870
We saw everything.

10:11.870 --> 10:14.140
Hey! Don't just blurt that—

10:14.140 --> 10:17.710
Memmeln, you want to summon
 the Ultimate Void, don't you?

10:20.710 --> 10:21.770
But why?

10:23.150 --> 10:26.720
We've been fighting 
together this whole time.

10:26.720 --> 10:31.290
Weren't we fighting the Voids 
together to protect the Last Town?

10:33.550 --> 10:34.490
I just...

10:35.640 --> 10:37.500
want it all to end.

10:37.780 --> 10:38.870
End?

10:39.350 --> 10:44.660
We elves live very long lives. 
Some even say we're eternal.

10:45.270 --> 10:48.810
I have seen many generations.

10:49.390 --> 10:52.620
Every generation 
would repeat some conflict,

10:53.010 --> 10:55.200
and I've lost many friends.

10:55.810 --> 10:57.870
All for the sake of peace.

10:58.280 --> 11:04.240
And I'm just going to continue living my life,
 fighting and losing my friends.

11:04.240 --> 11:05.420
For all eternity.

11:05.880 --> 11:12.140
But then, I found out there were people 
trying to summon the Ultimate Void.

11:12.620 --> 11:17.180
When the Ultimate Void appears, 
this world will end.

11:17.560 --> 11:22.180
I realized that our eternal extinction 
is what will lead us to true happiness.

11:22.560 --> 11:26.850
I want all of us to end together forever.

11:29.300 --> 11:30.790
That's shitty as hell.

11:31.900 --> 11:34.910
Seriously? How selfish can you be?

11:35.990 --> 11:40.620
I never imagined you of all people would be
 the selfish nuisance in the Nine Soldiers.

11:40.620 --> 11:42.740
The Memmeln I loved was nothing like that.

11:42.740 --> 11:44.610
The "me" you loved?

11:44.610 --> 11:48.020
Can you not force your selfish delusions
 on me? That's the <i>real</i> nuisance.

11:48.020 --> 11:48.820
And you, Memmeln?

11:49.730 --> 11:53.060
Don't you love all of the Nine Soldiers?

11:55.160 --> 11:58.600
If you do not understand, 
there is nothing I can do.

11:59.340 --> 12:01.820
I will let you all decide 
what you wish to do with me.

12:01.820 --> 12:03.190
Ah! Memmeln!

12:10.390 --> 12:12.070
Luke, what should we—

12:15.580 --> 12:18.970
Memmeln... It must've been so hard.

12:19.410 --> 12:21.850
She's lived so long and been so alone.

12:21.850 --> 12:23.350
<i>He's actually crying.</i>

12:25.280 --> 12:29.680
H-How dare you make Luke cry!
 You crazy monster!

12:29.680 --> 12:30.580
It wasn't me.

12:30.580 --> 12:32.590
I just got something in my eye.

12:42.570 --> 12:46.790
I heard the Soul Future's 
gotten bigger lately.

12:46.790 --> 12:47.830
Seriously?

12:47.830 --> 12:50.920
Just look at it. Doesn't it look 
even more brilliant lately?

12:50.920 --> 12:54.040
Maybe peace will finally be restored.

12:54.040 --> 12:57.460
It's all because the 
legendary hero and his friends

12:57.460 --> 13:00.360
are defeating the Voids 
and protecting this town.

13:03.600 --> 13:06.660
I hate tomorrow.

13:07.700 --> 13:13.480
How long is this hell going to continue?

13:14.820 --> 13:21.860
Please just end it already.

13:21.860 --> 13:28.220
Nothing... ness, ness, ness...

13:30.360 --> 13:34.550
Just a little more. Just a little more.

13:35.330 --> 13:37.550
I've thought up a plan to save Memmeln.

13:39.720 --> 13:43.430
When Memmeln tries to 
summon the Ultimate Void...

13:43.430 --> 13:46.750
Natsuko, you'll use your summoning 
spell and summon the Ultimate Void.

13:46.750 --> 13:48.940
"Live on! Now, disperse!"

13:48.940 --> 13:51.680
"Yes, Ultimate Void! As you wish!"

13:51.680 --> 13:56.020
Since they're believers of the Ultimate Void, 
they're bound to listen to whatever it says.

13:56.230 --> 13:57.140
What do you think?

14:01.160 --> 14:03.270
Hey, I thought real hard about that plan.

14:03.270 --> 14:05.530
I... I'm sorry.

14:05.930 --> 14:10.270
I mean, no one will get killed, so I guess 
mindless plans like this aren't so bad.

14:10.570 --> 14:12.240
It'll fail, but let's try it.

14:13.790 --> 14:14.580
But seriously...

14:16.150 --> 14:17.650
It's... It's so <i>bad</i>...

14:18.120 --> 14:19.780
Stop laughing!

14:25.020 --> 14:26.600
<i>Suspicious.</i>

14:31.890 --> 14:34.570
Ugh, it's no use.

14:35.690 --> 14:38.320
This is way better than what I drew.

14:38.320 --> 14:41.230
No, it needs more impact.

14:41.230 --> 14:43.190
I'm not sure that's necessary.

14:43.190 --> 14:46.460
Hm. But it really is.

14:46.730 --> 14:50.440
When I'm drawing, 
the whole world expands, like, "bam!"

14:50.440 --> 14:53.230
And sometimes, the characters 
start moving on their own.

14:53.230 --> 14:56.040
Oh, it's the moment they come to life.

14:56.040 --> 14:59.340
Whatever kind of villain they are,
the moment they're born into the world

14:59.340 --> 15:01.250
it's super impactful.

15:01.920 --> 15:05.130
Man, it's no use. Something's just off.

15:05.130 --> 15:06.920
I need to draw more.

15:06.920 --> 15:08.660
They're here. Hide.

15:15.930 --> 15:20.500
This thing's only ever reacted 
when Voids show up.

15:20.500 --> 15:22.180
I wonder if I'll be able to draw.

15:22.180 --> 15:25.060
If you can't, we'll just try again tomorrow.

15:25.310 --> 15:27.010
It's not like we'll die today.

15:30.240 --> 15:31.320
Yeah.

15:45.260 --> 15:48.840
Once you use your summoning magic
 and summon the Ultimate Void,

15:48.840 --> 15:51.510
I'll blend in with the believers
and incite them.

15:51.510 --> 15:52.540
Got it.

16:08.890 --> 16:13.610
Lady Memmeln has finally decided 
to go through with the final ritual.

16:13.610 --> 16:17.080
Yes. Once the hero who protects 
the Soul Future is gone,

16:17.080 --> 16:20.220
there'll be no one to stand in the way
 of summoning the Ultimate Void.

16:20.220 --> 16:21.560
The time has finally come.

16:21.560 --> 16:22.140
<i>Huh?</i>

16:23.070 --> 16:24.330
<i>Wait, what?</i>

16:29.510 --> 16:35.420
Ultimate Void. Please give me the strength,
 so I can come see you.

16:36.170 --> 16:39.250
I hate tomorrow.

16:39.250 --> 16:43.510
How long is this hell going to continue?

16:44.580 --> 16:50.640
Please just end it already.

16:50.640 --> 16:58.200
Nothingness! Nothing... ness, ness, ness...

16:58.500 --> 17:00.110
<i>Hey, hey, hey, hold on.</i>

17:00.510 --> 17:04.040
<i>That "What the hell?" moment is happening </i>now<i>?!</i>

17:04.440 --> 17:06.580
<i>So that was a Voidism ritual?</i>

17:07.510 --> 17:09.910
<i>But that means Memmeln 
was trying to kill Luke!</i>

17:09.910 --> 17:10.550
Lu—

17:11.840 --> 17:15.080
<i>No, no, no, no. If this goes
 like how it did in the movie...</i>

17:15.080 --> 17:17.460
<i>Luke's gonna end up killing Memmeln.</i>

17:17.460 --> 17:19.470
<i>Crap, crap, crap, crap.</i>

17:19.850 --> 17:20.850
<i>What do I do?</i>

17:20.850 --> 17:22.770
<i>What do I do? What do I do?</i>

17:24.110 --> 17:24.990
Draw.

17:25.350 --> 17:27.230
You need to draw, Natsuko.

17:27.230 --> 17:30.040
I know! But what do I draw?

17:30.040 --> 17:33.220
If I draw the Ultimate Void, it'd be like 
the real deal at an impersonator show,

17:33.220 --> 17:35.640
and it'll rile them up even more.

17:35.640 --> 17:38.930
Uh, I need <i>something</i>.

17:38.930 --> 17:41.240
Something that'll make 
Memmeln's heart skip a beat.

17:42.460 --> 17:43.580
That's it!

18:35.670 --> 18:38.050
Look! It's the Ultimate Void!

18:39.800 --> 18:41.570
The Ultimate Void?

18:44.970 --> 18:48.400
I'm the Ultimate Exister.

18:48.400 --> 18:49.420
What?

19:04.360 --> 19:12.510
<i>Reach out your hand 
and try to touch me gently</i>

19:12.510 --> 19:18.530
<i>This heart belongs to you</i>

19:19.020 --> 19:26.420
<i>I'll get rid of all of your pain</i>

19:26.420 --> 19:29.730
<i>This resonating heartbeat</i>

19:29.730 --> 19:36.910
<i>Believe in this melody of destiny</i>

19:44.280 --> 19:47.870
<i>I love today</i>

19:46.360 --> 19:49.910
<i>I love today</i>

19:48.260 --> 19:53.370
<i>We were able to meet 
because we're alive</i>

19:50.860 --> 19:53.370
<i>Because we're alive</i>

19:53.370 --> 20:00.900
<i>This heaven will last forever
 for the two of us</i>

20:00.900 --> 20:09.990
<i>Our story is about to start right now</i>

20:09.990 --> 20:19.140
<i>Fulfilled, filled, filled, fi-filled</i>

20:28.480 --> 20:29.740
Memmeln.

20:30.790 --> 20:33.580
This is just something I drew.

20:34.000 --> 20:37.740
But even if I die, 
this character will continue to live...

20:38.450 --> 20:39.870
for all eternity.

20:45.960 --> 20:47.380
Great job, guys.

20:52.820 --> 20:53.890
Memmeln.

20:59.200 --> 21:00.640
I...

21:02.630 --> 21:04.160
Let's go back together.

21:11.660 --> 21:15.670
Everyone in the choir has been infatuated 
with Sir Exister ever since.

21:15.670 --> 21:20.130
Yeah? By the way, this is Exister, 
one of the members in <i>Uta-Men</i>.

21:20.130 --> 21:21.200
<i>Uta-Men</i>?

21:21.200 --> 21:23.160
Singing Idol Men.

21:21.210 --> 21:29.220
<b>Uta-Men</b>

21:21.210 --> 21:29.220
<b>Uta-Men</b>

21:21.210 --> 21:29.220
<b>Broadcast Begins 7/2015!</b>

21:21.210 --> 21:29.220
Director: Mizuho Kawauchi
Series Composition: Nanami Hinata
Character Design: Shiori Sasaki

21:21.210 --> 21:29.220
<b>Express Your Excitement Through Song!</b>

21:23.160 --> 21:25.540
It was the first show I was an animator on.

21:25.540 --> 21:29.210
The animation director would yell at me 
every day, and I got super depressed, but...

21:30.030 --> 21:30.860
Here you go.

21:30.860 --> 21:32.320
Oh, my!

21:32.790 --> 21:36.740
If this makes you that happy, 
then I'm glad I did that job.

21:38.530 --> 21:40.200
You're okay now, right?

21:41.420 --> 21:47.020
Yes. Because I have all eternity 
to fangirl over Sir Exister.

21:49.270 --> 21:54.540
Oh, jeez. You should've told me 
earlier if all that happened.

21:54.810 --> 21:56.630
But I'm glad to hear it.

21:56.630 --> 22:00.250
And here I was, thinking 
you two were acting suspicious.

22:00.570 --> 22:02.080
Suspicious?

22:02.080 --> 22:05.290
I thought maybe you 
and Natsuko were dating.

22:06.200 --> 22:07.640
What're you talking about?!

22:07.640 --> 22:10.550
Unio! Jeez, you're such an idiot!

22:10.550 --> 22:12.980
There's no way! Me and Natsuko?

22:12.980 --> 22:16.240
Wait! Don't pick those yet!

22:13.760 --> 22:14.960
<i>You're kidding, right?</i>

22:15.980 --> 22:18.400
Wow. Just look at how much these have grown.

22:17.380 --> 22:18.980
Don't pick those, either!

22:18.400 --> 22:19.970
Uh, wait, I'll eat these!

23:49.990 --> 23:54.910
<b>Episode 5: "JUSTICE"</b>
